# Markdown is excluded deliberately. Prettier's only change to the docs here is
# padding table cells to a uniform width — 1920 lines of churn across 6 files,
# producing tables that are markedly harder to hand-edit than the compact ones
# already written. The prose itself is untouched (proseWrap defaults to
# "preserve"), so there is nothing to gain.
*.md

# Rewritten by `next dev` on every start — including the dev server Playwright
# boots for the e2e suite. Next reserializes it with one array element per line,
# which prettier --check rejects, so the file arrives unformatted through no
# action of the person running the tests. Formatting it back is not a fix: the
# next dev run undoes it. Committing Next's version is not one either, because
# Next also flips "jsx" from "preserve" to "react-jsx", which changes what the
# compiler does. Excluding it is the only option that does not churn, and there
# is nothing to gain from formatting a file no one hand-edits.
tsconfig.json
